@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<h1>About TaskFlow</h1>

<p class="lead">
    TaskFlow is a project tracking system built with ASP.NET Core MVC.
    It is designed to help users organize work into projects, boards, and tasks.
</p>

<div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h4>Purpose</h4>
        <p>
            The purpose of the application is to demonstrate a complete MVC web application
            with authentication, role-based authorization, Entity Framework Core data access,
            service-layer business logic, Razor views, Bootstrap design, AJAX, and unit tests.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-header">
                Main Features
            </div>

            <div class="card-body">
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li>User registration and login</li>
                    <li>Custom user entity</li>
                    <li>Administrator role</li>
                    <li>Project, board, and task management</li>
                    <li>Task comments</li>
                    <li>Task labels</li>
                    <li>AJAX task status update</li>
                    <li>Custom error pages</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-header">
                Technologies
            </div>

            <div class="card-body">
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li>ASP.NET Core MVC</li>
                    <li>ASP.NET Core Identity</li>
                    <li>Entity Framework Core</li>
                    <li>Microsoft SQL Server</li>
                    <li>Razor Views</li>
                    <li>Bootstrap 5</li>
                    <li>JavaScript Fetch API</li>
                    <li>NUnit tests</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mt-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h4>Architecture</h4>
        <p>
            The solution is split into multiple projects. The web project contains controllers
            and views, the data projects contain the database context and entity models,
            the services project contains business logic, and the test project contains
            automated service tests.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>